LRC reading: signed direction is a gauge symmetry for the observer,
but alternating signs convert many runner-runner clocks from differences
into pair sums.  For AP13 the opposite-sign clocks are exactly the odd
interior sums 3,5,...,25 inside C=27; the missing boundary shells 1 and
27 are the address tax that the observer projection erases.

UNIT-DISTANCE SHORT/UNIT/LONG TRIENERMENT PROBE
Rule: S(<1) follows base order, L(>1) reverses base order, U(=1) is a tie layer.

